  "co_occurrence_notes_HYPOTHESIS": [
    "deadpan pairs most often with understatement and sarcasm: flat delivery is the vehicle, understatement/sarcasm the content -- consistent with deadpan being a delivery-mode tag that layers onto a content-mechanism rather than a standalone joke type.",
    "absurdity pairs most often with misdirection and exaggeration: absurd content is frequently reached via a swerve (misdirection) or via inflating a real premise past the point of realism (exaggeration), suggesting absurdity is often the *result* of one of those two setup techniques rather than an independent structure.",
    "sarcasm pairs with exaggeration, irony, and rhetorical_humor at above-baseline rates, suggesting sarcasm in this corpus is usually delivered *through* one of these adjacent techniques rather than as bare tonal negation alone."
  ],
